WEBVTT

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.840
An AI agent with three

00:00:01.840 --> 00:00:03.740
ordinary permissions can be

00:00:03.740 --> 00:00:05.280
steered into leaking your data.

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:07.281
Read a public issue.

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:10.060
Read a private folder. Publish.

00:00:10.060 --> 00:00:12.880
No tool misbehaves. The

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:14.500
bug is the arrangement.

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:17.400
The arrangement is a path:

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:20.200
untrusted input, through the

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:22.820
agent's shared context, into private

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:24.480
data, and out to

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:26.660
a public sink. A list

00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:28.780
of tools cannot answer

00:00:28.780 --> 00:00:31.020
whether that path exists. A

00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:31.760
graph can.

00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:34.240
Lethal Path reads the M

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:35.820
C P config and

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:38.140
builds a graph: servers, tools,

00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:40.320
data, and the context

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:42.700
every tool shares. One Cypher

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:44.380
traversal anchors on that

00:00:44.380 --> 00:00:46.260
context and returns the route.

00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:48.620
Here: one route, four

00:00:48.620 --> 00:00:51.900
hops. Project folder, filesystem dot

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:54.500
read, context, git push,

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:56.840
public repo. The injection is

00:00:56.840 --> 00:00:57.981
a public GitHub issue,

00:00:58.540 --> 00:01:00.120
read into the same context.

00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:03.720
Now the fix. Lethal Path

00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:05.100
calls algo dot max

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:07.000
flow on Falkor D B.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:09.081
The engine returns flows,

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:10.920
not a cut, so Lethal

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:12.280
Path walks the residual

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:14.680
graph, compares both canonical cuts,

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:16.000
and picks the cheaper

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:18.940
one. Max flow two. The

00:01:18.940 --> 00:01:20.020
cut is the write

00:01:20.020 --> 00:01:22.520
side: revoke git push. The

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:24.180
same leak query re-runs

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:26.600
without it and returns zero

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:28.460
of one routes. Three

00:01:28.460 --> 00:01:30.600
of four declared tasks keep

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:32.520
working. That is the

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:32.960
receipt.

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:36.020
Now a real config, built

00:01:36.020 --> 00:01:37.180
from the official M

00:01:37.180 --> 00:01:40.020
C P server READMEs: GitHub,

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:43.400
filesystem, git. Forty tools

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:45.980
labelled by rule, zero unlabelled,

00:01:45.980 --> 00:01:48.380
secrets redacted before anything

00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:50.280
reaches the graph. Five hundred

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:51.461
and sixty seven routes.

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:53.740
The fix revokes nine write

00:01:53.740 --> 00:01:55.480
grants, and the re-run

00:01:55.480 --> 00:01:57.880
returns zero. This is not

00:01:57.880 --> 00:01:59.280
a bug report. It

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:00.640
is the arrangement of popular

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:02.040
tools, and it has

00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:03.020
hundreds of doors.

00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:05.680
The runtime guard watches the

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:07.140
same arrangement in a

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:08.700
live M C P session.

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:10.001
It reads the issue:

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:12.660
allowed. Reads the private folder:

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:15.940
allowed. Pushes: blocked, with

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:16.960
the route in the error.

00:02:16.960 --> 00:02:19.180
A fresh session, same

00:02:19.180 --> 00:02:21.780
push: allowed. The call did

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:23.740
not change. The arrangement

00:02:23.740 --> 00:02:25.360
did. The guard is a

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:27.580
demo: real M C

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:30.440
P stdio, simulated tool results.

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:34.080
Forty seeded configs with ground

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:37.261
truth by construction. Detection:

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:40.560
forty of forty. Fix cases:

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:43.080
forty of forty. Eight

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:46.520
clean configs, silent. The eval

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:48.560
is synthetic. It shows

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:50.000
the engine is consistent with

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:52.360
its spec, not accuracy

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:53.980
on every real setup.

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:56.860
Falkor D B is not

00:02:56.860 --> 00:02:58.180
a database behind this

00:02:58.180 --> 00:03:00.120
tool. It is the analysis:

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:02.100
the path query, the

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:04.120
max flow, the residual cut,

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:06.701
the verification. Remove it,

00:03:07.240 --> 00:03:08.580
and the route, the cut,

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:10.600
and the receipt stop

00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:14.000
existing. Lethal Path. Made by

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:15.200
Bhanu Nagpure.
